{"case_id":"T8021","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["API protocol","configuration","state"],"commit_induced":"YES","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":96,"affected_functions":["xmlCtxtSetErrorHandler","xmlCtxtErrMemory","xmlVErrParser","xmlParseBalancedChunkMemoryInternal","xmlCreateEntityParserCtxtInternal"],"reason":"S1 adds a public, context-specific error-callback protocol that H0 does not exercise. H0 defines xmlFuzzErrorFunc and allocation-failure controls, but never creates an xmlParserCtxt, calls xmlCtxtSetErrorHandler, controls errorCtxt, or verifies callback propagation into nested parser contexts. This is not merely the broad historical absence of a parser entry point: S0 had no xmlCtxtSetErrorHandler or xmlParserCtxt.errorHandler/errorCtxt state, while S1 introduces them and changes error dispatch and propagation around those identifiers.","evidence":["include/libxml/parser.h adds xmlParserCtxt.errorHandler and xmlParserCtxt.errorCtxt and publicly declares xmlCtxtSetErrorHandler.","parserInternals.c adds xmlCtxtSetErrorHandler and makes xmlVErrParser and xmlCtxtErrMemory prefer ctxt->errorHandler with ctxt->errorCtxt.","parser.c propagates the configured handler in xmlParseBalancedChunkMemoryInternal and xmlCreateEntityParserCtxtInternal, creating new nested-context behavior requiring configured state.","H0's xmlFuzzErrorFunc only discards errors; no H0 function calls xmlCtxtSetErrorHandler or supplies callback context data.","The many xmlErrMemory-to-xmlCtxtErrMemory changes are otherwise error-handling refactoring, but the newly configurable per-context callback and its nested propagation are externally controllable S1 behavior absent from S0."],"recommended_action":"Add or extend a parser fuzz target to create an xmlParserCtxt, install xmlFuzzErrorFunc or a state-checking structured callback through xmlCtxtSetErrorHandler, vary the callback data, and drive malformed, allocation-failing, and nested-entity inputs that exercise xmlVErrParser, xmlCtxtErrMemory, and handler propagation."}
